%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 4b3f2a8c8f344355b16a4d4296ae3f98, type: 3}
  m_Name: Rhino
  m_EditorClassIdentifier:
  vesselClass: 3
  entries:
  - Element: 1
    AbilityLabel: 'Sword Energy'
    AbilityDescription: 'Charge raises the energy the sword banks per cut - x1 at rest, x2 at level 10, floored at x0.5 (RhinoSkimmerDamagePrismEffectSO.chargeEnergyGainMultiplier on 0.04 per prism and 0.12 per super-shield). Energy lengthens the blade and pays for the energize (0.1 a time), so a charged Rhino refills both in half the cuts. Its own afterimages are prisms like any other: once the 1 s self-trail grace is past the blade cuts them and banks their energy.'
    Input: 13
    UnlockLevel: 5
    RelockBelowLevel: 4
    LatchPolicy: 0
    UpgradeLabel: 'Live Wire'
    UpgradeDescription: 'Once an energized blade''s stance is let go its 5 s tail runs out whatever the fingers do; with Live Wire every return to the chop stance re-lights it, so a blade kept coming back to the chop stays energized. ShieldSkimmerScaleConfigSO.liveWireUpgradeElement, gated on IsUpgradeActive(Charge) in ShieldSkimmerScaleDriver.'
  - Element: 2
    AbilityLabel: 'Afterimage'
    AbilityDescription: 'When the energized blade goes out, the sword keeps leaving copies of itself - prisms in the blade''s own shape and pose - for 5 s (RhinoSwordAfterimage, RhinoSwordAfterimageConfig). An omni-crystal surge lays them for its whole length. Mass scales their VOLUME: x1 at rest, x2.5 at level 10, floored at x0.25, read at the replicated level so every peer lays the same mass. They are not immune to the Rhino''s own blade: past the 1 s self-trail grace it cuts them like any prism.'
    Input: 13
    UnlockLevel: 5
    RelockBelowLevel: 4
    LatchPolicy: 0
    UpgradeLabel: 'Danger Afterimages'
    UpgradeDescription: 'The afterimages are laid as DANGER prisms (RhinoSwordAfterimageConfigSO.dangerUpgradeElement, gated on IsUpgradeActive(Mass), snapshotted per afterimage).'
  - Element: 3
    AbilityLabel: 'Blade Reach'
    AbilityDescription: 'Space lengthens the sword: the blade''s resting length runs 30 at rest to 50 at level 10 (Skimmer.Scale on the ForceFieldSkimmer Variant, read live by ShieldSkimmerScaleDriver), and stored energy grows it on top toward 120. Reach is what the blade cuts, what it strikes an Astro League ball with at the tip, and how far the afterimages reach.'
    Input: 13
    UnlockLevel: 5
    RelockBelowLevel: 4
    LatchPolicy: 0
    UpgradeLabel: 'Breaker'
    UpgradeDescription: 'The sword cuts a SHIELDED prism in one slice instead of two - the shield sheds and the core is cut in the same hit. Super-shielded prisms still need an energized blade. RhinoSkimmerDamagePrismEffectSO.breakerElement, gated on IsUpgradeActive(Space).'
  - Element: 4
    AbilityLabel: 'Ramp Spool'
    AbilityDescription: 'Time raises how fast the ramp boost winds the Rhino up to its top speed: 220 u/s per second at rest, 550 at level 10, 110 at the -5 floor (RampBoostActionSO.timeAccelerationMultiplier, x1 -> x2.5, floored x0.5, read live). It does not raise the ceiling - cruise 50 x maxBoostMultiplier 16.8 = 840 u/s - only how long the run-up takes. The Rhino is a bulldozer: its hull carries no prism slow, so ramming mass costs it no speed - the plough shoves what it hits aside (RhinoPloughPrismEffectSO) and the ramp keeps climbing through it.'
    Input: 0
    UnlockLevel: 5
    RelockBelowLevel: 4
    LatchPolicy: 0
    UpgradeLabel: 'Momentum'
    UpgradeDescription: 'Above 70% of top speed (588 u/s) danger prisms cannot drain the Rhino''s elements - the elemental-debuff ward scoped to DangerPrism alone, so an opposing pilot''s blast still lands (VesselElementalImmunity on the root, condition WhileAboveTopSpeedFraction, upgradeGate Time). The Time card lights while the ward is holding.'
